<title>BELGIUM: EU farm workers, employers sign jobs agreement.</title>
<headline>EU farm workers, employers sign jobs agreement.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>European farm workers and employers on Thursday signed a ground-breaking framework agreement to improve paid employment in the agriculture sector.</p>
<p>The voluntary agreement recommends a reduction in average weekly working hours by one hour to 39 hours and flexible contracts to cover training and parental leave as well as part-time, fixed-time, seasonal and temporary work.</p>
<p>It also calls on EU and national governments to penalise the use of illegal labour.</p>
<p>EU Social Affairs Commissioner Padraig Flynn welcomed the agreement.</p>
<p>In a statement he said it represented &quot;an important and concrete improvement in emplyment conditions for agricultural workers.&quot;</p>
<p>-Brussels newsroom +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
